User feedback on PR #236: *"minimum viable shipping has entered our
vocabulary again in this PR. that isn't okay. What would make it okay
is expanding our v0.20.x and v0.21.x plans, as they pertain, in both
our documents and the PR verbiage."*

This commit rewrites §17.4.2 (the ship sequence) and §17.4.3
(deliberately deferred) and §17.4.5 (recommendation) — plus tunes
§17.3 — to commit to full-coverage per-version deliverables rather
than minimum-viable subsets that defer "to see if anyone cares."

═══════ §17.4.2 expanded ship sequence ═══════

  v0.20.0 — Sol Geodetic Catalog ships ~38 bodies × 3 channels
            (gravity / topography / interior). Every body in v0.16.0
            52-body roster for which any spacecraft- or ground-based
            geodetic data has been published — including Voyager-only
            ice giants and single-flyby moons, with explicit honest-
            uncertainty flags rather than future-mission deferral.
            (was: "6 bodies × 3 channels = 18 entries")

  v0.20.1 — MagneticMultipoleCatalog ships full published roster
            including Mercury (Thébault 2018) and Earth EMM2017
            crustal field. NOT deferred to "v0.20.y once
            BepiColombo refresh." Sun synoptic state ships in
            parallel as bridge.get_solar_synoptic_state(jd_tdb).

  v0.20.2 — SolFluidInstrument ships ALL THREE Option-D layers
            together: climatological summaries + archive-pointer
            index + Earth/Mars state-at-epoch wrappers. Earth+Mars
            state-at-epoch NOT deferred to v0.21.x.

  v0.21.0 — SphericalHarmonicCatalog unification — concrete commit,
            scheduled on data-shape evidence from v0.20.x ships,
            not gated on "downstream consumer materialising."

  v0.21.1+ — Cross-channel coupling surfaces — three concrete
             couplings ship one per minor version (topography-
             gravity admittance; magnetic-multipole→dynamo;
             topography→atmospheric circulation).

═══════ §17.3 wording cleanup ═══════

Replaced "first floor" framing in three places (§17.3 intro,
§17.3.8 Scale-honesty, §17.3.8 Architectural-commitment):

  - §17.3 intro: "leave a tractable first floor on which a future
    contributor can build channel by channel" → "the v0.20.2 ship
